WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.610
- I hear you have a
serious connection with,

00:00:01.610 --> 00:00:04.330
like history with American
idol and I didn't know this.

00:00:04.330 --> 00:00:06.040
- Oh, yeah.

00:00:06.040 --> 00:00:07.980
- [Kelly] So, it's with
Jennifer Hudson, right?

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:08.813
- Yeah.

00:00:08.813 --> 00:00:10.300
- Wait, tell everyone
this. I didn't know this.

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:12.107
- They asked me to do
American idol and I said,

00:00:12.107 --> 00:00:13.220
"You now what I'd like to do?

00:00:13.220 --> 00:00:16.480
I'd like to give each of
the people on American Idol

00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:18.930
a new arrangement of
the song they picked."

00:00:18.930 --> 00:00:21.630
They wanted to do all of my songs.

00:00:21.630 --> 00:00:23.270
And I said, "Okay. You can do that."

00:00:23.270 --> 00:00:25.090
But I knew everybody
was going to ruin them

00:00:25.090 --> 00:00:26.486
if I didn't get my hands on them.

00:00:26.486 --> 00:00:27.942
(audience laughs)

00:00:27.942 --> 00:00:30.250
So I worked with each
one of them for a week.

00:00:30.250 --> 00:00:31.083
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:31.083 --> 00:00:33.720
- And I gave them all
different arrangements

00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:37.080
the way they wanted it
to. And they were great.

00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:38.190
Every one of them was great.

00:00:38.190 --> 00:00:40.367
And one of them was Jennifer Hudson.

00:00:40.367 --> 00:00:43.070
And she got bumped off that week.

00:00:43.070 --> 00:00:44.470
- [Kelly] Oh, the week
that she did your...

00:00:44.470 --> 00:00:47.870
- She did a great rendition
of "Weekend in New England".

00:00:47.870 --> 00:00:49.680
It was great working with all of them.

00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:51.160
- I think it's cool that you let them,

00:00:51.160 --> 00:00:53.330
'cause a lot of times they
don't let you be an artist.

00:00:53.330 --> 00:00:54.580
You're just singing other people's songs.

00:00:54.580 --> 00:00:56.700
I think it's cool that you
let them like, you know,

00:00:56.700 --> 00:00:58.280
cater to them, who they are as artists

00:00:58.280 --> 00:00:59.900
and like take your song...

00:00:59.900 --> 00:01:00.740
- I spent hours with them.

00:01:00.740 --> 00:01:02.490
- I know, that's what I'm
saying. That's really kind.

00:01:02.490 --> 00:01:04.110
And coming from that world

00:01:04.110 --> 00:01:05.270
and living in that world now with boys,

00:01:05.270 --> 00:01:06.410
not everybody does that.

00:01:06.410 --> 00:01:07.826
So it's really kind.

00:01:07.826 --> 00:01:10.790
- I put "I Made It Through
The Rain" on the piano

00:01:10.790 --> 00:01:13.700
and then just sing it the
way the piano player played.

00:01:13.700 --> 00:01:16.140
And I went, "No, let me help you.

00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:18.550
What do you wanna say with 'I
Made It Through The Rain'?"

00:01:18.550 --> 00:01:19.383
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:19.383 --> 00:01:20.216
- And then little by little,

00:01:20.216 --> 00:01:22.450
we would arrange the song for
each artist and it was great.

00:01:22.450 --> 00:01:24.070
- I think that's so special.

00:01:24.070 --> 00:01:24.925
(audience applauds)

00:01:24.925 --> 00:01:25.815
Just taking the time. That's so nice.

00:01:25.815 --> 00:01:27.405
Could you talk to Jennifer after that?

00:01:27.405 --> 00:01:30.610
- Well, after that, she
got pumped off that week

00:01:30.610 --> 00:01:34.600
and I was due to do this
Ryan Seacrest outdoor show.

00:01:34.600 --> 00:01:38.245
And I took her with me and I
was supposed to do two songs.

00:01:38.245 --> 00:01:41.365
I said, "You do the
second song, Jennifer."

00:01:41.365 --> 00:01:42.367
- [Kelly] Oh my God.

00:01:42.367 --> 00:01:43.200
- And I played the piano for her

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:46.354
doing "Weekend in New
England" on Ryan's show.

00:01:46.354 --> 00:01:47.187
- That's so nice.

00:01:47.187 --> 00:01:48.270
(audience applauds)

00:01:48.270 --> 00:01:49.103
- I loved her so much.

00:01:49.103 --> 00:01:51.180
- [Kelly] Yeah. Well, she did some things.

00:01:51.180 --> 00:01:52.760
- [Barry] Yeah.

00:01:52.760 --> 00:01:55.653
- You know how to choose 'em.
You should be an A&amp;R person.

